{
  "$comment": [
    "The canonical name of every concept the docs had started calling two things, and the spellings that must not come back.",
    "check-docs-vocabulary.mjs turns each entry into one lint rule per locale, so this file — not the script — is where the vocabulary is decided.",
    "`canonical` is a literal and has to appear on that locale's reference/glossary page; a test asserts it, so data and page cannot drift apart.",
    "`variants` are regular-expression sources, because a wrong spelling is often a substring of the right one or of an ordinary sentence.",
    "A page-name concept therefore matches the link-text form (`\\[…\\]\\(`): 「プラグインの管理方法」 is a fine sentence, while a link labelled 「プラグインの管理」 disagrees with the title of the page it opens.",
    "A term concept matches bare prose instead, since a second name for a term is wrong wherever it sits."
  ],
